namespace SaberWorkshop;
public static class TutorialContent {
 public static readonly string[] Titles={"Create a preset","Build from parts","Resize and move","Make a material","Create an outline","Trails and particles","Save and use"};
 public static readonly string[] English={
 "Press <b>New</b>, enter a name and choose <b>Straight</b> for a simple blade and handle. Press <b>Create</b>.\n\n<b>Outline</b> adds a dark shell and a coloured inner blade. <b>Segmented</b> starts with several sections; <b>Empty</b> starts with no parts.",
 "Your preset name and parts are on the left. Click a part to edit it.\n\n<b>Add part</b> creates a Blade, Handle, Ring, Particles or Trail. <b>Duplicate</b> copies the selected part in place. <b>Hide / show</b> changes visibility; <b>Delete</b> removes it.",
 "In <b>Part</b>, drag <b>Height</b>, <b>Width</b> or <b>Depth</b> to change size in millimetres. A short tap opens the numeric keypad. Expand <b>Ends and outline</b> to make the top or bottom <b>Flat</b> or <b>Pointed</b>, then adjust its tip length.\n\nExpand <b>Position and rotation</b> to place it. The preview starts at actual game size. <b>Center</b> resets its position. <b>View</b> opens zoom, reference mesh and test swing. <b>Actual size</b> restores 1:1 scale. The reference mesh is not exported.",
 "Open <b>Effects</b>. Choose a 2D texture, flowing plasma or 3D space. Edit the draft while watching the material card.\n\nChoose a sample shape and a target under <b>Apply material to</b>, then press <b>Apply to part</b>. Until then the saber stays as it was. <b>Save effect</b> adds the draft to your library. Check final bloom on the actual saber.",
 "Select a solid part. Expand <b>Ends and outline</b> and press <b>Create outline pair</b>. This creates a larger dark inverted shell and a smaller coloured inner part.\n\nSelect either part on the left and adjust its dimensions and colour independently. <b>Inverted faces</b> changes which side of a surface is visible.",
 "Use <b>Add part</b> to add a Trail or Particles.\n\nFor a trail, <b>Width</b> controls thickness, <b>Fade time</b> how long it stays in the air, and <b>Tail width</b> its taper. No texture files are required. Open <b>View</b> and turn on <b>Test swing</b>.\n\nFor particles, start with Sparks, Mist or Dust, then adjust rate, lifetime, speed and size.",
 "<b>Save</b> stores the editable Workshop preset. <b>Open</b> loads presets or saves a copy. <b>Undo</b> and <b>Redo</b> restore project edits.\n\n<b>View > Use preset in game</b> enables it for the next map. <b>Export CSL</b> builds a .saber under CustomSabers/Workshop. Export needs the configured Python and Unity Editor. Exporting edits to imported .saber files is currently paused."
 };
}
